      <summary>What is the Joint Development Model?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">A model where your team and ours develop the product together — shared requirements, co-engineering of design and process, and a common roadmap from prototype to volume.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>How is JDM different from a normal build-to-print order?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">Build-to-print starts from a finished design; JDM develops the design and the manufacturing process in parallel, so the product is manufacturable by design freeze.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>Who owns the IP in a joint program?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">Ownership is defined at the outset in the program agreement; customer IP is protected under NDA and secured under ISO 27001.</div>
    </details>
